# Versioned support claims

Before changing `packages/schema`, `packages/compiler`, `packages/runtime`, `packages/canvas-renderer`, `packages/motionscript-emitter`, or `docs/languages`:

1. Read `packages/schema/capabilities/releases.json`.
2. Read the current MotionScript and Scene IR version files it names.
3. Read `docs/languages/compatibility-policy.md` and the root `AGENTS.md`.

Published version files are immutable. Support claims change only together with the registry, tests, and the pending or new version entry. Evaluation reports describe one revision; they are not the specification.

Wire strings (`0.1`, `0.2`) are coarse family ids. Consumers distinguish additive schema features with the fuller language release id in `releases.json` and with `requiredCapabilities` / `requires`. Completing a capability already published is a package bump only. A pending construct such as `geometry.pathMorph` needs a new version entry. Details: `docs/languages/compatibility-policy.md`.

Evaluation Baselines pin `git rev-parse HEAD` (clean tree) or a complete source snapshot. Link the pin and results from the work item.

Follow the current root AGENTS.md, charter and owning workstream direction. Capability changes need live task justification; consequential alternatives and new execution models need a bounded recorded decision. Preserve valid versioning and scoped conformance requirements.
